  "goodToKnow": "Infrage (also in Frage) appears in two set phrases. Infrage kommen means to come into consideration: Er kommt für den Job infrage, and Das kommt nicht infrage! means that's out of the question, a parent's classic. Infrage stellen means to question or challenge: Sie stellt die Entscheidung infrage. Since the 2006 spelling reform, both infrage and in Frage are correct. Similar: zurzeit, zuliebe."
